index 0000000..3cc242d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0026-bert-text-pairs.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,389 @@
+llama: a BERT reads a text pair's second segment on token-type row 1 (pair_segments), and a BERT sequence classifier keeps its pooler
+
+A BERT trained on text pairs reads `[CLS] a [SEP] b [SEP]` with the first
+segment's tokens on token-type row 0 and the second's on row 1 - Hugging
+Face's token_type_ids. The graph gave row 0 to every token ("token types are
+hardcoded to zero"), so such a model read its second segment as more of the
+first. Measured on ncbi/MedCPT-Article-Encoder (title, abstract) against
+NCBI's own usage (transformers, fp32, CPU), 67 PubMed pairs: cosine as low as
+0.9736 with every token on row 0; 0.9999882 at worst with the segments.
+
+llama_context_params::pair_segments (default false; common_params too): the
+BERT graph then gives a token after its sequence's first [SEP], by position,
+row 1 (src/llama-pair-segments.h: read off the ubatch's tokens, each
+sequence its own first separator). A single text, `[CLS] a [SEP]`, is all
+row 0, as before. The caller builds the pair and refuses a first segment that
+holds a [SEP] of its own. A context asking it of a model that is not BERT, has
+no second token-type row or no separator is refused at creation, never run
+with the pair dropped. Without pair_segments the graph is the one it was.
+
+The converter dropped BERT's pooling layer ("we are only using BERT for
+embeddings"), for BertForSequenceClassification too, whose score is
+classifier(tanh(pooler.dense([CLS]))): the classifier read the raw [CLS]
+row, and ncbi/MedCPT-Cross-Encoder's logits were off by up to 16. The pooler
+is now the head's dense layer (cls, tanh by default) for a sequence classifier
+of BertModel itself; every class built on it still drops it. With both,
+MedCPT's cross-encoder scores 80 (query, article) pairs within 0.079 of
+torch's logits.
+
+MedCPT's tokenizer is registered for its pre-tokenizer hash
+(convert_hf_to_gguf_update.py, `medcpt`, WPM; llama-vocab reads no
+pre-tokenizer for WPM): without it the converter stops on "BPE pre-tokenizer
+was not recognized".
+
+Not changed: the residual against torch (cosine 1 - 1.2e-5, logits 0.08) is
+ggml's tanh GELU against BERT's erf GELU, on every BERT here alike; moving
+BERT to ggml_gelu_erf would move every BERT space's vectors and belongs to a
+new space, not to this patch.
+
+Checked: tests/test-bert-pair-segments.cpp, standard library only, 8 cases;
+both MedCPT models converted with this tree, embedded and scored through the
+gRPC server on CPU against torch (the outer patch's numbers).
